module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one type variable is bound by two actuals of distinct types (variants of two different coproducts, or Int and Bool) and the program is Accepted.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: a non-generic f(a: P) called with Q1 is refused (TypeMismatch Coproduct(P) vs Coproduct(Q)). Constructor expressions already elaborate to the owner coproduct. The hole was generic rebind, not variant-to-coproduct typing.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5 / section 4b values inhabit declared types). Two inhabitants of unrelated coproducts share one type variable.",

    "AUTHORED ON THE V1 .dag AND NOW EXECUTED ON THE SEED (review 80480; superseded at the 2751b200 seed regeneration of #14152). v1.compiler.infer unify_generics returns UnifyGenericsAcc and names a later actual that node_type_equals rejects, and the shipped mirror src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs now carries that same fold (its unify_generics returns Rc<UnifyGenericsAcc> and emits the two-leg diagnostic (v1.compiler.infer unify_generics rebind-branch diagnostic construction, mirrored in src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs)). The pre-regen state described below was true of fa06f6b45ca and is false of 2751b200.",

    "RUNG, STATED HONESTLY (review 81093 finding 2; DESIGN section 4b meta-obligation 1, the reported rung equals the rung established by EXECUTED evidence): the fold's refusal was ESTABLISHED ONCE BY EXECUTION and its REGRESSION IS UNENFORCED. Both halves are load-bearing and the second is not a hedge.",

    "WHAT THE FIRST HALF MEANS, precisely. On head 2751b200 the four reject controls were run twice with the seed's execution as the only variable (both seed variants shipped as files, because the runner's git base is not the PR head and `git checkout <ref> -- path` there silently writes base content -- it produced one fake RED before this was caught). Against the pre-regen seed fa06f6b45ca: same_arm_two_distinct_coproducts_refuses_with_the_fold_message FAILED, same_arm_int_bool_refuses_with_the_fold_message FAILED, applied_constructor_same_head_differing_argument_list_refuses FAILED, probe_one_t_two_coproducts_compiles_to_a_refusal FAILED. Against the regenerated seed: all four ok, with every accept control ok on BOTH sides (int/int, same coproduct, Box<Int> twice, List<Int> twice, lambdas, Option, Outcome, and the probe's both-P1 control). The controls assert the fold's OWN diagnostic shape -- 'bound as' plus '(first argument)' plus '(later argument)', the rebind-branch expected/got construction of v1.compiler.infer unify_generics -- so they cannot go green on a fold that never emits it. Matched on shape rather than on a variable letter because the fold names the generic's own name: a hardcoded 'T' made the Box<Int> vs Box<Bool> row read green on both seeds while the fold was in fact refusing it under the name A, which is a near-miss that would have made a passing row look like a failing one.",

    "WHY THAT IS NOT A STANDING RUNG 3. Those controls are Rust tests, in src/v1/tests/src/cross_coproduct_generic_locate_test.rs and src/v1/tests/src/cross_coproduct_probe_discharge_test.rs, and the tree already declares that no required lane runs Rust unit tests: gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn deleted the rust-unit-tests job with the other v1-judged required lanes, and gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_pull_requests (Superseded by that same ruling) records that a unit-test red is found nowhere on the required path. DESIGN's Building & checks section says it plainly: nothing on the required path evaluates a witness or runs the v1 unit tests. So a later edit that re-introduces first-wins binding -- in v1.compiler.infer, in the shipped seed, or in what 05_emit_rust.dag emits -- turns no required check red. Reporting rung 3 as standing would present a measurement taken once, by hand, on a runner, as if it were still being produced. The measurement is real; the enforcement is absent, and it is absent by a declared ruling, not by accident.",

    "THE DECLARED DROP IS A ROW, NOT PROSE (review 81093 finding 1): see gunbc.rung_drop.unify_generics_rebind_unenforced_on_emitted_and_required_paths (dag/gunbc/rung_drop/, DESIGN section 4b meta-obligation 3). It carries both arms -- the emitted tree, which no gate reads, and the required path, which runs neither the Rust controls nor a discriminating claim -- with the restoration capability for each. The earlier version of this receipt declared the drop as a String inside its own receipts list; every other drop in the tree is a file in that directory, and DESIGN section 4c puts a restoration condition in a typed carrier rather than in prose.",

    "WHAT IS CLAIMED, THEREFORE, IN ONE LINE: the fold executes today, the controls that prove it execute nothing tomorrow, and the class's rung across its in-scope paths is the MINIMUM (DESIGN section 4b meta-obligation 1) -- which is what the rung_drop row states as Mitigatable for both the emitted and the required path. WHAT A TYPE NAME OR A .dag FOLD ESTABLISHES IS NOTHING: the .dag fold has been in the tree since 8f8f92f80c1 and established nothing until the seed carried it and a discriminating RED executed against it. The next rung-raising step is not another red; it is putting this red where a required gate runs it, which the rung_drop row's restoration trigger names.",


    "RESIDUAL, NOT THIS CLIMB: ConstructorTag<P> {} == ConstructorTag<Q> {} is still Accepted. That is operator follow-up C, not a green control of this class. NEXT TRIGGER for C: a typecheck refusal of that equality (or a declared reason it is a different class). A SECOND ROUTE, ALSO OPEN AND UNFIXED, IS NAMED SO IT IS NOT MISTAKEN FOR A RUNG: 'type A = B' makes alias A and alias B equal by RHS equality, and alias_rhs_of_decl returns None for a NON-LEAF rhs (src/v1/04_types.dag), so a chain stops there. The two known_red_probe rows on alias_route_probe_red in dag/gunbc/explicit_witness_admission.dag are THAT class and were not discharged here; do not read the discharge below as covering them.",

    "QUARANTINE GONE FOR THE V1 COPY ONLY (dissolved at 2751b200, DESIGN section 4b meta-obligation 4: The RED stays enrolled, the quarantine goes). The dissolve_on wording of the v1 known_red_probe row on constructor_tag_route_probe_red (dag/test/claim copy) named two conjuncts, and both now hold on the shipped seed: (a) v1_compiler_infer.rs unify_generics returns UnifyGenericsAcc -- true at 2751b200 (36 occurrences; 0 at fa06f6b45ca); (b) the probe refuses rather than being first-wins Accepted. For (b) the probe source is compiled verbatim by src/v1/tests/src/cross_coproduct_probe_discharge_test.rs::probe_one_t_two_coproducts_compiles_to_a_refusal, which requires the refusal to BE the rebind refusal rather than any blocking diagnostic, with probe_same_tag_side_by_side_is_still_accepted as its positive control. THE V2 COPY STAYS ENROLLED (review 81163 finding 1; review 81191 finding 1; section 4b meta-obligation 1, the minimum across paths): src/v2/test/claim/manual/constructor_tag_route_probe_red.dag::same_arm_one_t_two_coproducts_must_refuse and its known_red_probe row are NOT dissolved by this PR -- #14152 repairs v1.compiler.infer unify_generics and the seed mirror only and touches no file under src/v2/compiler, so the v2 route (v2.compiler.infer infer_match_generic_formal) is unrepaired and its RED keeps its evidence slot; the v2 identity stays in gunbc.rung_drop transitional_admission_exception. A String-returning print (v2.test.claim.manual.cross_coproduct_generic_locate locate_v2_infer_print) asserts nothing and cannot go red, so it is not the v2 replacement (section 5). WHY THE V1 ROW LEAVES AND ITS TEST STAYS: a runtime bool claim cannot discharge a compile-time exit condition -- the witness returned false at both heads, because a compile refusal at the call makes the whole module fail to compile and the claim never reaches a verdict; and no scheduled executor runs the QuarantineProbeExpectRed batch: the cadence is read by gunbc.quarantine_probe_disposition, which derives from it WHICH mechanism holds a probe's red obligation, but no workflow under .github/workflows executes rows in it (no cargo test or claim_batch step anywhere in it), so a row left in that cadence is a ledger entry nothing runs -- the same gap gunbc.rung_drop transitional_admission_exception enrols other rows for. The former dag/test/claim/constructor_tag_route_probe_red.dag is deleted; accept controls stay in test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate. Defect cases are still not merge-checked as blocking_count == 0.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "unify_generics", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_same_coproduct_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_int_int_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_two_applied_box_int_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_two_distinct_coproduct_values_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.manual.constructor_tag_route_probe_red", decl_name: "same_arm_one_t_two_coproducts_must_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_int_bool_values_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate", decl_name: "same_arm_nested_two_distinct_coproduct_values_refuse", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
